# LF in the working tree on every platform, Windows included.
#
# Git for Windows checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` by default, which is
# what `actions/checkout` gets on a windows-latest runner. `gofmt` treats a
# file with CRLF line endings as unformatted, so the first Windows leg of
# .github/workflows/ci.yml reported every single .go file in the repository as
# needing `gofmt -w` — a wall of noise with one cause and nothing to do with
# the code (ark:rein#11).
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf, so this fixes the developer's checkout too: Go
# source is LF, and a Windows contributor should not have to know that.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except things that are not text. `text=auto` already leaves detected binaries
# alone; these are named so a new one is not misdetected the day it lands.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
